  <h2 id="what-each-exam-is">What CUET and EAMCET actually are, for a PCB/BiPC student</h2>

  <p>
    CUET-UG (Common University Entrance Test) is a national exam run by the National Testing Agency. It started as the admission route for central universities and has since been adopted by a large and growing list of state and private universities as well.
  </p>

  <p>
    EAMCET, now formally called EAPCET, is not one exam but two state-level exams: AP EAPCET for Andhra Pradesh and TS EAPCET for Telangana. Both split candidates into an MPC group (Maths, Physics, Chemistry, mainly engineering-bound) and a BiPC group (Biology, Physics, Chemistry, mainly pharmacy, agriculture, and life-science-bound).
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--amber">
    <p class="callout__eyebrow">Where the confusion starts</p>
    <ul class="callout__list">
      <li>CUET is national and multi-university; EAMCET/EAPCET is state-specific to Andhra Pradesh and Telangana.</li>
      <li>Neither exam is the same as NEET, even though BiPC/PCB students sit a biology-heavy paper for all three.</li>
      <li>A CUET score is not one universal cutoff — each participating university reads it differently for its own programs.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="callout__footer">
      Get this distinction right before you plan your whole year around either exam.
    </p>
  </div>

