  <h2 id="eamcet-engineering">Can BiPC students do B.Tech through EAMCET?</h2>

  <p>
    Mostly no, and this is one of the most-asked, most-misunderstood questions BiPC students bring to EAMCET.
  </p>

  <p>
    Standard B.Tech admission through EAPCET is built around the MPC-group paper, which tests mathematics directly. A BiPC student's paper does not include the same maths content, so most engineering branches stay closed by default.
  </p>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      A small number of colleges do admit BiPC candidates into specific branches — commonly biotechnology, pharmaceutical engineering, or agricultural engineering — through a mandatory bridge course in mathematics completed after admission.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is a limited, college-specific concession, not a standard, guaranteed path. Availability changes by year and by institute, so confirm directly with the specific college and the state counselling authority before you plan your whole strategy around it.
    </p>
  </div>

